Chapter: TowerPlanSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Frame
  cites Safari chapter Tower
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter DepthSort
  cites Safari chapter TowerPlan
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 TowerPlan: which lattice masts are worth showing, and which segment each one
 belongs to.

 A SEGMENT CAN CARRY TWO TOWERS AND MOST CARRY ONE. Every segment has an exit
 tower beyond its far end; a LONG one also gets a mid-tower halfway along and on
 the other side of the road. Grading the counts on a chain with no long segment
 and again on one with a long segment is what separates the two rules -- a
 chapter that gave every segment both would agree with this everywhere except the
 count.

 THE TWO TOWERS ON ONE SEGMENT MUST NOT BLINK IN STEP, which is why the mid-tower
 is keyed at its segment index PLUS SIXTY rather than at its index. Sixty is half
 the beacon period, so the pair are in exact antiphase -- and grading the two
 offsets is what says the key is different at all. A chapter keying both on the
 segment would put two beacons on one stretch of road flashing together.

 THE TOWER JUST BEHIND HIM IS THE ONE THE CHAIN CANNOT REACH. The chain starts at
 the rider's current segment and only runs forward, so the previous segment's
 exit tower -- which is still in view over his shoulder on a corner -- is added
 separately, through the mapper that steps FORWARD across the join instead of
 back. It appears only when there is a previous segment.

 We say:

Section: The Constants

  fixed-got : List Real
  fixed-got = [tower-beyond, tower-right, seg-tower-left]

  fixed-want : List Real
  fixed-want = [160.0, 20.0, 100.0]

  cap-got : List Integer
  cap-got = [max-vis-towers]

  cap-want : List Integer
  cap-want = [16]

Section: One Tower Per Segment

 The route's first three segments are all under the mid-tower length, so each
 contributes exactly one.

  segs : List Segment
  segs = [segment-at 0, segment-at 1, segment-at 2]

  chain : List Integer
  chain = [0, 1, 2]

  origin : Pose
  origin = Pose { along = 0.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, hw = 2.0 }

  short-got : List Integer
  short-got =
    [ list-length (walk-towers segs chain origin 0),
      list-length (seg-towers segs chain origin 0),
      list-length (seg-mid-tower segs chain origin 0),
      list-length (all-towers segs chain origin 0) ]

  short-want : List Integer
  short-want = [3, 1, 0, 3]

  mid-flags-got : List Boolean
  mid-flags-got =
    [ (list-at segs 0).has-mid-tower, (list-at segs 1).has-mid-tower, (list-at segs 2).has-mid-tower ]

  mid-flags-want : List Boolean
  mid-flags-want = [False, False, False]

 The exit tower stands a hundred and sixty metres beyond its segment's end and
 twenty out from the lane edge, in that segment's own frame.

  where-got : List Real
  where-got =
    let t = list-at (seg-towers segs chain origin 0) 0
    in let u = list-at (seg-towers segs chain origin 1) 0
    in [t.a0, t.x0, u.a0, u.x0]

  where-want : List Real
  where-want = [660.0, 22.0, 480.0, 22.0]

Section: Two On A Long One

 Segment 6 is twelve hundred metres and carries a mid-tower as well: one beyond
 its end, one halfway along and on the OTHER side of the road.

  long-segs : List Segment
  long-segs = [segment-at 6]

  long-got : List Integer
  long-got =
    [ list-length (walk-towers long-segs [0] origin 0),
      list-length (seg-mid-tower long-segs [0] origin 0) ]

  long-want : List Integer
  long-want = [2, 1]

  long-where-got : List Real
  long-where-got =
    let ts = walk-towers long-segs [0] origin 0
    in [ (list-at ts 0).a0, (list-at ts 0).x0,
         (list-at ts 1).a0, (list-at ts 1).x0,
         (list-at ts 0).yaw, (list-at ts 1).yaw ]

  long-where-want : List Real
  long-where-want = [1360.0, 22.0, 600.0, -98.0, 0.5235987750000001, 0.0]

Section: The Beacon Keys

 The exit tower is keyed on its segment; the mid-tower on that plus sixty, which
 is half the blink period -- so the pair on one segment are in antiphase and
 never flash together.

  key-got : List Real
  key-got =
    let ts = walk-towers long-segs [0] origin 0
    in [ (list-at ts 0).off, (list-at ts 1).off,
         beacon-offset-for 0, beacon-offset-for 60 ]

  key-want : List Real
  key-want = [0.0, 60.0, 0.0, 60.0]

 Three different segments get three different offsets, which is the whole point
 of a stride coprime to the period.

  spread-got : List Real
  spread-got =
    let ts = walk-towers segs chain origin 0
    in [(list-at ts 0).off, (list-at ts 1).off, (list-at ts 2).off]

  spread-want : List Real
  spread-want = [0.0, 37.0, 74.0]

Section: Behind And Beyond

 The previous segment's tower is added only when there is one, and it is an
 addition to the walk rather than part of it.

  behind-got : List Integer
  behind-got =
    [ list-length (all-towers segs chain origin 0),
      list-length (all-towers segs chain origin 1),
      list-length (all-towers segs chain origin 2),
      list-length (behind-tower segs chain origin 0) ]

  behind-want : List Integer
  behind-want = [3, 4, 4, 1]

 A tower whose base centre is at or behind the near plane is not collected at
 all -- it sorts by that centre, so there would be nothing to sort it by.

  cull-got : List Integer
  cull-got =
    [ list-length (walk-towers segs chain (Pose { along = 5000.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, hw = 2.0 }) 0),
      list-length (walk-towers segs [] origin 0) ]

  cull-want : List Integer
  cull-want = [0, 0]

Section: Into the Frame

  items-got : List Integer
  items-got =
    let ts = walk-towers segs chain origin 0
    in let its = tower-items ts 0
    in [list-length its, (list-at its 0).i, (list-at its 2).i, list-length (tower-items [] 0)]

  items-want : List Integer
  items-want = [3, 0, 2, 0]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tl-fixed " fixed-got fixed-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "tl-cap   " cap-got cap-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "tl-short " short-got short-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "tl-mid   " mid-flags-got mid-flags-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tl-where " where-got where-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "tl-long  " long-got long-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tl-lwhere" long-where-got long-where-want 0.000000000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tl-key   " key-got key-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "tl-spread" spread-got spread-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "tl-behind" behind-got behind-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "tl-cull  " cull-got cull-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "tl-items " items-got items-want)
  end
